1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,093
Think it through.

2
00:00:01,093 --> 00:00:07,187
Nothing can happen until there is a cambial ring, so first the ray cells dedifferentiate.

3
00:00:07,187 --> 00:00:09,518
That event creates the meristem.

4
00:00:09,518 --> 00:00:12,473
Then the new cambium makes secondary xylem.

5
00:00:12,473 --> 00:00:16,549
As the wood builds up, the primary phloem is crushed.

6
00:00:16,549 --> 00:00:22,539
Only once the cortex is stretched does the cork cambium form and make lenticels.

7
00:00:22,539 --> 00:00:27,382
And tyloses come last of all, in old wood turning into heartwood.

